                <pb facs="0141" n="59" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg59"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 158.931/89b.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the American
                    Minister.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-02-11"><hi rendition="#italic">February 11,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Dr. Strong and his assistant, Dr. Oscar Teague, will leave Manila for Peking by
                    the first available transportation, and are to be introduced to the Chinese
                    Government as having been sent by the American National Red Cross, the usual
                    agency of the United States in such matters. Mr. Wilson instructs Mr. Calhoun to
                    inform the Chinese Government that the services of these gentlemen are placed
                        <pb facs="0142" n="60" xml:id="pg60"/> at its disposition in response to
                    China’s invitation to this Government to send specialists.</p>
            </div>
